  Franka Emika Robot (FER, FCI v5), arm only, mesh-free. Generated file: see
  `tools/fer-model-fit` and `docs/book/src/reference/model.md`; do not edit by hand.

  Joint origins and axes: `franka_description`'s `fer_joint1..8`, which agree with
  the robot's own `libfcimodels_x64.so` to 4e-16.

  `<inertial>` elements: identified from that shared object by the `fit` command of
  `tools/fer-model-fit`, as the minimum-norm correction to `franka_description`'s
  published values that reproduces the library's mass matrix and gravity torques.
  Regressor rank 45 of 70 (the classical base parameters), worst residual 3.553e-14 over
  208 joint configurations.

  These ten numbers per link are a base-parameter-equivalent set, NOT a physically
  meaningful description of each casting: some moments of inertia are negative. That
  is a property of the robot's own model, not of the fit — no exact fit is physically
  consistent (the smallest reachable pseudo-inertia eigenvalue over the whole family
  of exact fits is -1.496e-2). Use this file to reproduce libfranka's numbers, not to
  seed a physics simulation.

  Link names are libfranka's own `link0..link8`, because `franka::model::NativeBackend`
  looks for the flange under `RobotModel::kLastLinkName`.
-->
